  "followups": [
    {
      "date": "2026-09-19",
      "author": "Claude Fable 5.1 (second reviewer)",
      "status": "Step 1 root cause not demonstrated; character of the variance established; WebGL2 bit-repeatable; gate change PROPOSED, not adopted; nothing blessed",
      "method": "qa/pages/repeat.html?sequence=1 (36 poses × 2 cold iframe loads) in (a) visible Safari and Brave windows and (b) Brave 153 --headless=new with WebGPU (ANGLE Metal), several instances concurrently; new rig flags &stall, &backend, &noblob passthrough; qa/frame-compare.mjs for per-pair metrics.",
      "findings": [
        "Safari 26.6 WebGPU (visible window): 5/36 pose pairs differ — the variance is not specific to Chromium/Dawn.",
        "Brave 153 visible: 2/36 differ (both T2, whole-frame bounds, one at maxDelta 1).",
        "Headless WebGPU across 14 sequence runs: 22/504 pairs differ (≈4.4%); plain control runs and perturbed runs (warm=90, stall=300 ms×3 frames, --disable-gpu-shader-disk-cache, noblob) all show the same intermittent behaviour, so warm-up length, load-time stalls, the shader disk cache and the contact-blob pass are each excluded as the cause. The rate rose with more concurrent instances (GPU contention), which points at a timing-dependent per-load state inside the WebGPU path.",
        "Headless WebGL2 (same three.js scene, ANGLE Metal) across 5 sequence runs: 0/180 pairs differ — bit-repeatable in every pose and tier.",
        "Ink render target (?scene=inkrt&p=0.64, R/G view) across 8 headless cold loads: one hash (0db1e995…) — the once-per-load ink pass is excluded as the cause.",
        "Character of a differing pair (38 saved pairs, build/step1-pair-metrics-2026-09-19.jsonl): changed pixels ≤ 1.55% of the frame, median ΔE76 of changed pixels ≤ 0.94 (sub-threshold), worst 5×5 block mean ΔE76 ≤ 2.9; the whole-frame cases are 1–3 level scatter consistent with ulp-level shading differences flipping the 1/255 dither; the lettering cases are edge speckle; one historical T3 pair contains a single star pixel flipping at a glyph edge (ΔE 72 for one pixel, 5×5 block 2.9)."
      ],
      "excluded_causes": [
        "ink RT (8/8 identical)",
        "contact blob (noblob runs differ)",
        "warm-up length (warm=90 differs)",
        "load-time stalls (stall=300 differs)",
        "GPU shader disk cache (disabled, differs)",
        "Chromium-specific (Safari differs)",
        "MSAA/env/shadows/derivatives/bias/centroid (Codex 09-07…09-11)",
        "CPU-side uniform/vertex/index/storage bytes and shader strings (Codex gpuTrace, equal)"
      ],
      "proposal_requires_owner_authorization": {
        "summary": "Keep bit-exact SHA-256 references for the WebGL2 backend (demonstrated repeatable) and for every pose where WebGPU cold loads reproduce; gate WebGPU frames against blessed PNGs with a tolerance derived from the observed variance, so a real regression (moved lettering, changed gold, lighting shift) still fails while ulp-level scatter passes.",
        "tolerance_candidate": {
          "changedPct_max": 1.0,
          "dE76_p50_max": 1.0,
          "worstBlock5x5DE76_max": 4.0,
          "note": "derived from 38 observed pairs with margin; the 1.55% pair (0.86-T2) would need changedPct_max 2.0 or a re-capture policy (best of two loads)"
        },
        "not_done": "No reference hash changed, no PNG blessed, no gate altered. M7/M8 remain open."
      },
